{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49122","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:53.678757+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"MEMBER","body":"Internal reproducer submitted in cl/985244532.","created_at":"2026-09-21T13:47:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/49122#issuecomment-5761531365","id":5761531365,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49122","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABV2n95Q","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/5761531365/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-09-21T13:47:06Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/5761531365","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/194224583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/penumallas1261","id":194224583,"login":"penumallas1261","node_id":"U_kgDOC5Ohxw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"## Summary\n\nFor a `dynamic-slice` whose result is partitioned along the sliced dimension and whose start index is out of range, the SPMD partitioner emits `partition_id * shard_size + clamp(raw_start, 0, dim − slice_size)`, i.e. it clamps the raw start against the whole operand and then adds the shard offset. `DynamicSlice` semantics clamp the *global* start first (here 7 → 2) and each result shard then reads its own piece of that window (starts 2 and 5). The emitted starts are 5 and 5, so both shards return the same last columns. Unsharded compilation and NumPy are correct. Similar to #49118 (dynamic-update-slice). \n\n## Reproducer (CPU only, 2 host devices)\n\n```python\nimport os\nos.environ[\"XLA_FLAGS\"] = \"--xla_force_host_platform_device_count=2\"\nos.environ[\"JAX_PLATFORMS\"] = \"cpu\"\nimport numpy as np, jax, jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import lax\nfrom jax.sharding import NamedSharding, PartitionSpec as P\n\nmesh = jax.make_mesh((2,), (\"x\",), devices=jax.devices(\"cpu\")[:2])\ncols = NamedSharding(mesh, P(None, \"x\"))   # shard the sliced (column) axis\nrep  = NamedSharding(mesh, P())\n\ndef f(x, start):\n    return lax.dynamic_slice(x, [jnp.int32(0), start], (2, 6))\n\nx = jnp.arange(16, dtype=jnp.int32).reshape(2, 8)\nstart = jnp.int32(7)                        # out of range: clamps to 8 - 6 = 2 -> columns 2..7\nexpected = np.asarray(x)[:, 2:8]\n\nuns = np.asarray(jax.jit(f)(x, start))\nsh  = np.asarray(jax.jit(f, in_shardings=(cols, rep), out_shardings=cols)(x, start))\nprint(\"unsharded:\", uns[0].tolist(), \"ok\" if np.array_equal(uns, expected) else \"WRONG\")\nprint(\"sharded:  \", sh[0].tolist(),  \"ok\" if np.array_equal(sh, expected) else \"WRONG\")\n```\n\n```\nunsharded: [2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7] ok\nsharded:   [5, 6, 7, 5, 6, 7] WRONG\n```\n## Agent Analysis\n\nPost-partitioner HLO for the result-shard slice:\n\n```\n%multiply = %partition-id * 3\n%clamp    = clamp(0, %raw_start, 5)        ; clamps against the 8-wide operand (8 - 3)\n%start    = %multiply + %clamp\nROOT dynamic-slice(%global_value, 0, %start), dynamic_slice_sizes={2,3}\n```\n\nFor raw start 7 the clamp gives 5 on both partitions, and the surviving dynamic-slice's own clamp into `[0, 8 − 3]` keeps 5 for both. The correct order is `clamp(raw_start, 0, 8 − 6) = 2`, then `2 + partition_id * 3` → `[2, 5]`. Code: the partitioned-dimension dynamic-slice path in `SpmdPartitioningVisitor::HandleDynamicSlice`, `xla/service/spmd/spmd_partitioner.cc`.\n\n","closed_at":null,"closed_by":null,"comments":1,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49122/comments","created_at":"2026-09-19T21:47:58Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49122/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/49122","id":5513823228,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","id":4409976544,"name":"bug","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABBtrm4A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/bug"},{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"008672","default":false,"description":"Awaiting response from openxla-eng","id":4409976552,"name":"stat:awaiting openxla-eng","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABBtrm6A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/stat:awaiting%20openxla-eng"},{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Related to XLA on CPU","id":4432378339,"name":"CPU","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABCDC54w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/CPU"},{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"B04E1E","default":false,"description":"Related to sharding","id":8390615212,"name":"sharding","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAAB9B6grA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/sharding"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49122/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_i